    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Taxation",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5280             Revised 04/11/2017\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act in relation to a certain agreement for a payment in lieu of\ntaxes\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nThis bill relates to a certain agreement for a payment in lieu of\ntaxes with respect to a lessee that is a qualified empire zone\nenterprise of certain real property.\n\n SUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Makes provisions for payment in lieu of taxes made by a\nqualified entity for a specific property\n\nSection 2. Allows the qualified entity to make a claim for a credit or\nrefund for tax years 2012-2015.\n\nSection 3. Effective Date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nQualified Empire Zone Enterprises (QEZE) are vital businesses which\nencourage job growth and foster economic development. During the\nrelevant years, the Qualified Company paid rent to a limited liability\ncompany, formed for the sole purpose of acquiring and holding this\nproperty, through a qualified exchange, which is an affiliate of the\nQualified Company by common ownership and control.  Due to a\ntechnicality involving these commonly owned and controlled companies,\nthe Department of Taxation and Finance will not honor the QEZE tax\ncredit. As a result, the Qualified Company, which had been approved\nfor a tax credit and had been audited by the state during the relevant\ntime period, was later denied the credit. Furthermore, Tax and Finance\nis attempting to claw back the credit from prior years.\n\nThe business has complied with the law and has relied on this tax\ncredit for operating expenses. This bill would allow the property\nowner to receive their tax credit for the years 2012, 2013, 2014 and\n2015. In 2014, two similar pieces of legislation were signed into law.\nIn 2016, another similar piece of legislation was signed into law.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately and shall apply to taxable years beginning on or after\nJanuary 1, 2012 and before January 1, 2016.\n",
